  const file = this.files[0];

  // Read the selected file
  reader.readAsText(file);
});
```

In this example, we first create a new `FileReader` object which will handle reading our file asynchronously. We then define a callback function that gets executed once the file has finished loading. Inside this callback, we split the CSV text into individual lines and process each line further by splitting it into columns based on commas.

To use this script, you need to add an HTML element where users can select their CSV files:

```html
